    "result_text": "Green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: a create is rejected with **409** when the requested city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `EnsureHouseholdUnique` duplicate-check pattern), I added:\n\n1. **`EnsureCityCapacity`** (`.../rest/function/owner/EnsureCityCapacity.java`) \u2014 reads the validated request via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitive, trimmed) via `OwnerRepository.findAll()`, and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50. It runs before `save`, so the new owner isn't self-counted.\n\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** (checked, `extends Exception`) with a `CAPACITY = 50` constant.\n\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with body `{\"errors\":[\"city\"]}`, consistent with the other duplicate/conflict handlers.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n\n5. Wired **`ensureCityCapacity`** into `owners.POST.yml` after `ensureUniqueHousehold` and before `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the neighboring steps.\n\nThe pre-existing acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a fresh city to 50, expect the 51st to be a 409) passes, and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures/errors).",
